  "duration": 39,
  "text": "Malik chose a table near an outlet, opened his laptop, and pulled up the family budget he had finished three nights ago. He only meant to check one thing. Then he found the mistake. The repair estimate for his mother's car had been entered in the monthly column instead of the emergency-expense column. Correcting it pushed the August balance below zero. Not far below zero. But zero did not care how close you came. He stared at the red number as students entered around him in bright shirts, fresh sneakers, and the nervous confidence of people pretending not to look for somewhere safe to sit. That spreadsheet looks like it just told you a family secret.",
